# Check every text file out with LF on every platform.
#
# test/cases.js corrupts a rule on purpose to prove a broken rule is reported
# rather than answered as "release", and it finds that rule by matching a
# literal \n. On a CRLF checkout that match fails and the test reports that it
# could not break the knowledge base. Pinning the line ending keeps the suite
# honest on Windows, where Git converts to CRLF by default.
* text=auto eol=lf
